course: dictionary
lesson: 5361
title: A bird with a clue in its name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A kingfisher is a bird, and its name holds a clue. A fisher is someone who catches fish, so a kingfisher is a bird that catches fish. Always check the word parts first, then read the sentence to see if your idea fits.
explain: Read the clues in «The kingfisher dives head-first from a perch and its dagger beak enters the water with little splash.» Dives, perch, beak and water tell you what the bird does and where it does it. You can picture the bird before you know every word.
explain: The name does not always match the bird's food. «African pygmy kingfishers are tiny kingfishers that mostly hunt insects in woods, not fish in rivers.» The word «not» is a clue that warns you. Read the whole sentence, not just the one word you know.
fact: A kingfisher is a small, brightly coloured bird with a big head and a long, sharp beak.
fact: Common kingfishers dive into water to catch fish.
fact: Some kingfishers, such as the kookaburra, are large and catch lizards, insects and snakes on land.
fact: «Kingfisher blue» is a bright blue, named after the bird.
fact: Japanese engineers copied the kingfisher's beak shape to make a bullet train quieter and faster. This is called biomimicry.
exercise: «The kingfisher dives head-first from a perch.» What does dives mean here? | Sits still | *Plunges down quickly | Flies backwards | Sings loudly
exercise: Which bird is called a big kingfisher whose family groups laugh together at dawn? | Robin | *Kookaburra | Heron | Owl
exercise: In «African pygmy kingfishers are tiny kingfishers», which word tells you they are small? | insects | woods | African | *tiny
test: What does the word kingfisher mean? | A bird that only lives in cities | A fish that flies | *A bird that catches fish | A bird that lays eggs in a nest
test: «Japan's bullet train was given a kingfisher-shaped nose.» Why did the engineers do this? | To make the train float | To make the train red | *To make the train quieter | To make the train fly
exam: Which sentence about kingfishers is true? | Kingfishers never dive | *Some kingfishers hunt insects in woods, not fish in rivers | Kingfishers have no beak | Every kingfisher lives in a city
